2026-07-22 16:51:05.021 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.mobile.MobileUIController - xsol xsol system guide y plan wiring diagram jun 2013 v2 0 y plan wiring diagram select a demand below for an animation of the operational sequence heating only hot water only heating amp hot water heating on hot water satisfied hover your mouse pointer over the text for more information about that component important note the red lines show only where power is required for correct operation they do not represent all of the live wires in the system always follow the appropriate safety procedures before starting any work on the system hw on ch on hw off s1 s2 room thermostat mid position motorised valve cylinder thermostat programmer boiler 3amp fused spur common satisfied calling pump grey or brown white orange blue n sends power to the cylinder stat common sends power to the room thermostat common sends power to the mid position valve grey wire note not all y plan systems use the hw off terminal of the programmer if this is the case the programmer must be set to turn on both heating and hot water when heating is selected gravity mode rs1 555 700 n neutral l common from programmer heating on 3 heating calling to the white or brown in some valves wire of the mid position valve this powers the valves motor moving it to its mid position rs2 555 708 3 wire 3 calling to the white or brown in some valves wire of the mid position valve this powers the valves motor moving it to its mid position 2 wire 2 calling to the white or brown in some valves wire of the mid position valve this powers the valves motor moving it to its mid position mid position valve head 555 312 body 555 321 diverts the flow of water according to the demand wiring colours grey hot water off white or brown heating on orange power to pump and boiler blue neutral cylinder thermostat 555 730 terminals of cs1 c common from hot water on of programmer 1 calling for hot water to pump and boiler 2 satisfied to grey wire of mid position valve supplying voltage required to fully open programmer 555 111 terminals of up2 l live 1 hot water off 2 heating off not normaly used 3 hot water on 4 heating on warning during a heating and hot water demand the grey wire will be live there will be approximately 80vac on this wire when measured to earth this voltage is a back feed from the valve and is used to hold the valves motor in the mid position vertical scroll bar 2 pages horizontal scroll bar 2 pages 0
