2026-07-22 19:58:08.341 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.mobile.MobileUIController - xsol electrical insulating mat 2017 v4 part no t00461 the mat provides an insulated barrier over electrically live connections to enable safe access to components when carrying out tests on an appliance the mat can also be used when working on a pcb to protect it from damage and water spillage even though the appliance is isolated the mat has the added advantage of being transparent which allows easy identification of test points shown in xsol as the whole area can still be seen note the electrical insulating mat is for use during testing only the mat shall not be used to allow working on an appliance when in an unnecessary electrically live condition isolate mains power to appliance as per tops p4 how to use carefully position the insulating mat over exposed live components amp connections the mat can be easily flexed or folded to allow for good positioning take care not to disturb any electrical or water connections whilst positioning the mat ensure the mat is secure and maintains its intended position between the electrical connections and your hands etc during testing energise the appliance once the mat is securely in position perform your tests taking care not to disturb the position of the insulating mat and adopting safe working practices at all times on completion of the tests isolate the electrical supply before the mat is removed care amp inspection the mat should be kept clean dry and free from debris before use inspect for signs of damage or splits do not stack heavy items on top of the mat as this may cause damage if damage is apparent do not use and replace immediately vertical scroll bar 2 pages horizontal scroll bar 2 pages carefully position the insulating mat over exposed live components amp connections the mat can be easily flexed or folded to allow for good positioning take care not to disturb any electrical or water connections whilst positioning the mat ensure the mat is secure and maintains its intended position between the electrical connections and your hands etc during testing energise the appliance once the mat is securely in position perform your tests taking care not to disturb the position of the insulati 0
