2026-07-22 19:58:41.762 [TestNG-tests-1] INFO  core.controller.mobile.MobileUIController - xsol check for external mixing poor hot water no fault codes boiler looks to be working properly maybe only one tap affected this could be a faulty mixer tap or shower passing cold water into the hot supply after the boiler there are a couple of ways to check for this which we will run through here method 1 is to isolate the boiler from the cold mains water supply then open the hot tap as if you were draining the hot water circuit after a short time the tap should run dry if it does not then there is quot something quot passing method 2 is to measure the temperature of the hot water pipe below the boiler and compair it to the temperature of the water leaving the problem tap step 1 measure the temperature of the hot water pipe at the boiler record the result of the temperature measured step 2 run the hot water tap untill the temperature stableases then measure the temperature of the water at the tap record the result of the temperature measured step 3 compare the two readings the temperature at the tap should be similar to the output from the boiler if the temperature at the tap is significantly cooler than at the appliance this would indicate that external mixing is occurring it is sometimes possible to hear the faulty valve passing go round all of the mixers and listen for water flow if pracical isolate the suspect valve and restore the cold supply to the boiler to confirm 2017 v6 vertical scroll bar 2 pages horizontal scroll bar 2 pages 0
